{
	"info": {
		"_postman_id": "or-import-run-readback-2026-11-25",
		"name": "OpenRegister Import Run Read-back API",
		"description": "An import run read back after it finished, with its failing rows and their reasons (change runs-recorded-and-causes-named, task 4.4; REQ-RCN-005 and REQ-RCN-006).\n\nA CSV of three rows is previewed and committed into a schema that requires a name and counts in integers: one row is written, one is refused for the missing name and one for a text count. The run is then read back: its file, fingerprint, policy, actor and counts; its rows with the written row naming the object it created and the refused rows their reasons and submitted values; the failing rows as CSV led by _row and _reason; the created object's audit entry naming the run as its cause; and a retry with the corrected rows as a new run naming the original, which stays unchanged.\n\nThe two CSV files sit next to this collection and are uploaded by relative path, like test-import.csv in the crud collection. Import runs are records and have no delete route, so the two runs stay; the object, register and schema are removed.",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
	},
